{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall declare.</b> A term of raising the voice (Sotah 32)." "<b>An Aramean sought to destroy my father.</b> He recalls the kindnesses of the Omnipresent: אֲרַמִּי אֹבֵד אָבִי — Laban sought to uproot everything when he pursued after Jacob, and because he intended to do it, the Omnipresent reckoned to him as though he had done it — for the Holy One, blessed be He, counts the intent of the nations of the world as deed (see Sifrei)." "<b>And he went down to Egypt.</b> And yet others came upon us to destroy us — for after this, Jacob went down to Egypt." "<b>With few persons.</b> In seventy souls (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:24.398995452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}